SWEET boot line 1024 (patch 0176, research 108): arm64 BOOT_LINE_LENGTH 608 -> 1024 (the i386 value of the same tree, pexpert/pexpert/i386/boot.h:76), so struct boot_args grows from 736 to 1152 bytes and the boot-args line holds 1023 characters instead of 607. No iBoot in this port: the shim (shim/loader.c, BOOT_LINE_LENGTH 1024, static asserts on the layout; payload version 2) is the only producer and changes in the same commit; tools/mkpayload.py and tools/run-preflight follow. Readers use the macro (kern_sysctl.c, kern_stackshot.c, IONVRAM.cpp) or the struct fields (start.s via genassym BA_BOOT_FLAGS, arm_vm_init.c memSizeActual). osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c carries the string "SWEET_BOOT_LINE_LENGTH=1024" (from the macro) and tools/mkpayload.py refuses a kernel without it (review bootline-1024-r1 F1). Host test tools/test_bootline_layout.py. Not run on hardware.

